Z||000000||black-86-GT||11-04-2000||12:33 PM||||the headlight motor relay went out on my 87 gt and since there are not ANY GT's in the local junk yard and a new one costs like 147 bucks. Does anyone know if one from a firebird or trans am will work or they are any cheaper new. any help is always apprciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-04-2000||01:35 PM||||I've got some.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||11-04-2000||01:39 PM||||I believe that ones for Trans-Ams, and Firebirds for the same time frame will work fine. Look at the junk yard for them, you can usally find them for like $2.00. I heard that some time ago on here. Its not a relay, its an electronic conrol module. Check around at junk yards because the ones for the other cars will be just as much new.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">   <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>If you smoke after sex, your doing it way to fast.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||11-04-2000||01:52 PM||||Seanh is right - the 1987-later Fieros and Firebirds use a control module, instead of relays...  <B>much</B> better than the old relay system.<P>BTW, you say there aren't any GTs in your salvage yard.  But it doesn't have to be a GT - just 1987 or later.  On Fieros, they're tucked inside the LF fender, ahead of the wheelwell, as you probably already know.  The ones on Firebirds are on a bracket near the brake master cylinder, and are much easier to get to.   ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DavidHenshaw||11-04-2000||07:06 PM||||I bought an exact replacement relay at Advance Auto for about $18.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||11-04-2000||07:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DavidHenshaw:<BR><B>I bought an exact replacement relay at Advance Auto for about $18.<P>Dave<P>86 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Was it for your 86 GT?? If so thats not the same thing. 84-86 are diffrent than 87-88.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000006||theogre||11-04-2000||08:11 PM||||The headlight controller for 87 & up fiero is also used on other GM cars. Specifically the sunbirds with the little half door. The controller is mounted on the left shock tower in the sunbird. (I saw one today. I knew I should have grabbed it.....)||||reg||1
Z||000007||black-86-GT||11-06-2000||06:17 PM||||wow thanx guys i really appreciate it. And you are right it is a modual not a relay. But i will definetley check out the junk yards around here tomorrow. And no not only are there no GT's around there are no 87 or 88 fieros around here either. Once again thanx for the help.||||reg||1
